 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Depends on the situation. If the pipes frozen, you want to thaw them. If there's a smell, you might have a broken line. Then you' cleaned the pipes, and that's handy. Still, it' worth checking the tank and draining it completely a couple times a season. Don't. Pack them snugly and give them to someone with a dumpster, or bury them off the path in the deep woods. Birds will thank you. There are few basics, and they save a lot of grief. You' already ahead by asking. Now go find a spot under the stars.",
